From 91bdf03450d1fac2d941dce52fa4fe7ea980114c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Noa Himesaka <himesaka@noa.codes>
Date: Tue, 24 Nov 2026 13:26:55 +0900
Subject: [PATCH 08/14] usb: ehci: add MStar/SigmaStar FUSBH200 glue and a port
 reset hook

Add the MStar flavour of the Faraday FUSBH200 EHCI (ehci-fotg210.c from
linux-chenxing, Kconfig symbol renamed to USB_EHCI_FUSBH200 so it does
not collide with 7.3's fotg210 driver) and the ehci.h/hcd hooks it uses.

Add an optional ehci->port_reset_hook called around root port reset.
SSD20xD uses it for what the vendor's patched usb core does: lower the
chirp K detection level (UTMI 0x2a = 0x80) and the eye settings during
reset, restore the disconnect level at the first status poll and the
eye settings afterwards. Without it high speed devices enumerate at full
speed only.

Also fix probe returning an uninitialised retval when the usbc syscon
is missing, convert .remove to return void, and add the vendor UHC ECO
bits for sstar,ssd20xd-ehci.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
